  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 602.27 Landscaping",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 602.27 “Landscaping” means the planting of non-invasive ornamental or native plant species in planting beds created by hand or placement by hand of ornamental items such as small sculpture or statuary, stepping stones or stone edging within planting beds, all occurring in a previously altered area, such as lawn, within the developed coastal buffer. The term includes gardening.\n\nSource. #12806, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html"
